=== yt ===
yt [version]
Command line interface for JetBrains YouTrack

Usage: yt [FLAGS] <SUBCOMMAND>

Commands:
  api         Send a request to the YouTrack REST API and print its JSON
              response
  article     Work with knowledge base articles
  auth        Sign in and manage credentials
  board       Work with agile boards and sprints
  completion  Print a shell completion script
  config      Show and change settings
  issue       Work with issues
  profile     Manage profiles (a YouTrack instance and an account)
  project     Work with projects
  time        Log and list spent time
  help        Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)

Flags:
      --profile <PROFILE>  Profile to use [env: YT_PROFILE]
      --format <FORMAT>    Output format (default: table) [env: YT_FORMAT]
                           [possible values: table, json, ndjson]
  -v, --verbose            More log output: -v for debug, -vv for trace
  -q, --quiet              Only print errors
      --no-color           Disable color
      --no-input           Fail instead of prompting [env: YT_NO_INPUT]
  -y, --yes                Confirm destructive actions without asking
  -h, --help               Print help
  -V, --version            Print version

=== yt auth ===
Sign in and manage credentials

Usage: yt auth <SUBCOMMAND>

Commands:
  login   Sign in to a YouTrack instance
  logout  Sign out: delete the stored credential
  status  Show which profile is used and whether its sign-in works
  help    Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)

Flags:
  -h, --help               Print help

Global flags:
      --profile <PROFILE>  Profile to use [env: YT_PROFILE]
      --format <FORMAT>    Output format (default: table) [env: YT_FORMAT]
                           [possible values: table, json, ndjson]
  -v, --verbose            More log output: -v for debug, -vv for trace
  -q, --quiet              Only print errors
      --no-color           Disable color
      --no-input           Fail instead of prompting [env: YT_NO_INPUT]
  -y, --yes                Confirm destructive actions without asking

=== yt auth login ===
Sign in to a YouTrack instance

Usage: yt auth login [FLAGS] [URL]

Arguments:
  [URL]  YouTrack URL, e.g. https://acme.youtrack.cloud

Flags:
      --method <METHOD>    How to sign in
                           [possible values: browser, token]
      --client-id <ID>     OAuth client ID from your YouTrack administrator
                           [env: YT_OAUTH_CLIENT_ID]
      --token-stdin        Read a permanent token from stdin
      --no-browser         Do not open a browser; finish by pasting the address
                           instead
      --revocable          Also allow `yt auth logout` to revoke this sign-in on
                           the server (shown to you as "YouTrack Administration"
                           access)
  -h, --help               Print help

Global flags:
      --profile <PROFILE>  Profile to use [env: YT_PROFILE]
      --format <FORMAT>    Output format (default: table) [env: YT_FORMAT]
                           [possible values: table, json, ndjson]
  -v, --verbose            More log output: -v for debug, -vv for trace
  -q, --quiet              Only print errors
      --no-color           Disable color
      --no-input           Fail instead of prompting [env: YT_NO_INPUT]
  -y, --yes                Confirm destructive actions without asking

