=== yt issue ===
Work with issues

Usage: yt issue <SUBCOMMAND>

Commands:
  attachment  Work with issue attachments
  command     Apply a YouTrack command to issues
  comment     Work with issue comments
  create      Create an issue
  delete      Delete issues
  edit        Change issues
  link        Work with issue links
  list        List issues matching a YouTrack query [aliases: ls]
  show        Show an issue
  tag         Add or remove issue tags
  help        Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)

Flags:
  -h, --help               Print help

Global flags:
      --profile <PROFILE>  Profile to use [env: YT_PROFILE]
      --format <FORMAT>    Output format (default: table) [env: YT_FORMAT]
                           [possible values: table, json, ndjson]
  -v, --verbose            More log output: -v for debug, -vv for trace
  -q, --quiet              Only print errors
      --no-color           Disable color
      --no-input           Fail instead of prompting [env: YT_NO_INPUT]
  -y, --yes                Confirm destructive actions without asking

=== yt issue create ===
Create an issue

Usage: yt issue create [FLAGS]

Flags:
  -p, --project <PROJECT>   Project short name
  -s, --summary <TEXT>      Summary
  -b, --body <TEXT>         Description (Markdown)
      --body-file <PATH>    Read the description from a file, or `-` for stdin
  -f, --field <NAME=VALUE>  Custom field: NAME=VALUE (repeatable)
      --dry-run             Show what would be created without creating it
      --no-validate         Skip client-side field validation
  -w, --web                 Open the new issue in the browser instead of
                            printing its URL
  -h, --help                Print help

Global flags:
      --profile <PROFILE>   Profile to use [env: YT_PROFILE]
      --format <FORMAT>     Output format (default: table) [env: YT_FORMAT]
                            [possible values: table, json, ndjson]
  -v, --verbose             More log output: -v for debug, -vv for trace
  -q, --quiet               Only print errors
      --no-color            Disable color
      --no-input            Fail instead of prompting [env: YT_NO_INPUT]
  -y, --yes                 Confirm destructive actions without asking

=== yt issue edit ===
Change issues

Usage: yt issue edit [FLAGS] <ID>…

Arguments:
  <ID>…  Issue IDs or URLs; `-` reads IDs from stdin

Flags:
  -s, --summary <TEXT>      New summary (one issue)
  -b, --body <TEXT>         New description (one issue)
      --body-file <PATH>    Read the description from a file, or `-` for stdin
  -f, --field <NAME=VALUE>  Custom field: NAME=VALUE, NAME+=VALUE, NAME-=VALUE,
                            or NAME= to clear (repeatable)
      --dry-run             Show the changes without applying them
      --no-validate         Skip client-side field validation
  -h, --help                Print help

Global flags:
      --profile <PROFILE>   Profile to use [env: YT_PROFILE]
      --format <FORMAT>     Output format (default: table) [env: YT_FORMAT]
                            [possible values: table, json, ndjson]
  -v, --verbose             More log output: -v for debug, -vv for trace
  -q, --quiet               Only print errors
      --no-color            Disable color
      --no-input            Fail instead of prompting [env: YT_NO_INPUT]
  -y, --yes                 Confirm destructive actions without asking

