=== yt api ===
Send a request to the YouTrack REST API and print its JSON response

Usage: yt api [FLAGS] <PATH>

Arguments:
  <PATH>  Path under /api, e.g. `issues/WEB-1` or `admin/projects?$top=5`

Flags:
  -X, --method <METHOD>    HTTP method
                           [possible values: GET, POST, DELETE]
                           (default: GET)
      --input <FILE>       JSON request body from a file, or `-` for stdin
      --fields <SELECTOR>  `fields` selector to add to the query
  -h, --help               Print help

Global flags:
      --profile <PROFILE>  Profile to use [env: YT_PROFILE]
      --format <FORMAT>    Output format (default: table) [env: YT_FORMAT]
                           [possible values: table, json, ndjson]
  -v, --verbose            More log output: -v for debug, -vv for trace
  -q, --quiet              Only print errors
      --no-color           Disable color
      --no-input           Fail instead of prompting [env: YT_NO_INPUT]
  -y, --yes                Confirm destructive actions without asking

